    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nRVSec reports `KeyGeneratorSpec` for `HmacSHA1` because that CrySL rule's allowlist does not include the Android-supported `HmacSHA1` `KeyGenerator` algorithm. This is a rule-policy mismatch rather than an Android API defect.\r\n\r\nThe generated key material is used by the existing HmacSHA1-based master-secret implementation. Changing only the key generator to HmacSHA256 would not change the MAC algorithm or improve security, and could obscure the established 160-bit master-secret layout. This revision retains `HmacSHA1` and explicitly initializes the generator to the existing 160-bit MAC-key size.",
