      "created_at": "2026-10-17T22:06:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-17T22:07:50Z",
      "body": "Thanks for the feedback. RVSec reports `KeyGeneratorSpec` because its permitted algorithms are `AES, HmacSHA256, HmacSHA384, HmacSHA512, HMAC-SHA256, HMAC/SHA256, HMAC-SHA384, HMAC/SHA384, HMAC/SHA512, HMAC-SHA512`; `HmacSHA1` is absent. This is a CrySL policy restriction rather than an Android API defect, and changing only the generator provides no security improvement, so my PR revision retains `HmacSHA1` and explicitly initializes its existing 160-bit key size.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
